{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And I will set a sign among them.</b> This sign is for disgrace, because of lack of sight, and the sign is a novelty such as nothing like it has been seen." "The meaning of <b>the fugitives</b> is that most of them will die, as is explicit in the book of Ezekiel (Ezekiel 38:21–22, 39:11 and following) and in the book of Zechariah (Zechariah 14:12, 18)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:21.461321519Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}